/*
 * The port's stylesheet.
 *
 * recompui loads this by name from <executable>/assets/recomp.rcss during
 * renderer bring-up (ui_state.cpp: init_styling). It is not optional: if the
 * file is missing, the frontend throws while building its menus, and because
 * that happens on the renderer thread the exception crosses a noexcept boundary
 * and the process fail-fasts with exit code 0xC0000409 and no message at all.
 *
 * It is deliberately almost empty. recompui carries its theme in code as a
 * palette of named colours, and its elements style themselves from that. A port
 * that writes its own colours here does not restyle those elements, it competes
 * with them. So this file supplies the one thing the library cannot know --
 * which font to use -- and otherwise stays out of the way. Restyling belongs in
 * C++, by setting theme colours, not in rules added here.
 *
 * The family name is the one declared inside the .ttf, not its filename:
 * LatoLatin-Regular.ttf calls itself "LatoLatin". It must match what
 * src/main.cpp passes to register_primary_font. Getting it wrong fails quietly
 * and confusingly -- every element lays out and draws in the right place, with
 * no text in any of them.
 */

body {
    font-family: LatoLatin;
    font-weight: normal;
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 20dp;
}
